{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Test 7","h":0.013670313625088526,"c":1,"y":0.072379959444151543,"x":0.10275817487926235,"w":0.061973361968994153},{"h":0.013081395583944611,"t":"B","w":0.014403292338053389,"c":1,"x":0.10493827142356589,"y":0.45348837184465562},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"D","x":0.10493827185527031,"y":0.77616279048668213,"c":1,"w":0.018518517812093099},{"w":0.23251027425130205,"y":0.11627906936465893,"h":0.023296902120745311,"t":"Flying tortoises","c":1,"x":0.40534979992853276},{"y":0.15842167236945315,"t":"An airborne reintroduction programme has helped conservationists take","x":0.18106995690594818,"w":0.67901234944661448,"h":0.015996932421752708,"c":1},{"t":"significant steps to protect the endangered Galápagos tortoise.","y":0.17447137926753353,"h":0.018916225545678844,"x":0.22216318471611154,"c":1,"w":0.59681157430013021},{"c":1,"t":"Forests of spiny cacti cover much of the uneven lava plains that separate the","x":0.14808492372197132,"y":0.20959556333180718,"h":0.019047819121847165,"w":0.72646830240885418},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.22965116264430174,"c":1,"t":"interior of the Galapagos island of Isabela from the Pacific Ocean. With its","x":0.14814815151150051,"w":0.69958847045898442},{"h":0.019400694344995695,"x":0.14806748555002419,"y":0.24587836846375521,"c":1,"w":0.73473592122395837,"t":"five distinct volcanoes, the island resembles a lunar landscape. Only the thick"},{"x":0.14809742417695634,"h":0.018652338021214354,"y":0.26339848668964061,"t":"vegetation at the skirt of the often cloud-covered peak of Sierra Negra offers respite","c":1,"w":0.79022059122721344},{"y":0.28343023241230214,"w":0.7654320780436199,"h":0.016039732066986834,"t":"from the barren terrain below. This inhospitable environment is home to the giant","x":0.14814815840617362,"c":1},{"h":0.01744185965530165,"c":1,"x":0.15020577056982223,"t":"Galápagos tortoise. Some time after the Galápagos's birth, around five million","w":0.73251027425130222,"y":0.29941860488165151},{"c":1,"x":0.1478975385328882,"y":0.31395522436579326,"t":"years ago, the islands were colonised by one or more tortoises from mainland","w":0.73701024373372392,"h":0.024222411031015301},{"h":0.018998480797937201,"t":"South America. As these ancestral tortoises settled on the individual islands, the","w":0.75525304158528639,"y":0.33429376054762872,"c":1,"x":0.15015106412355503},{"t":"different populations adapted to their unique environments, giving rise to at least","x":0.15020577259478859,"y":0.35306242661440002,"w":0.75925923665364581,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"w":0.76954732259114589,"h":0.016010628150966877,"y":0.37209302310990422,"x":0.15020576247445727,"c":1,"t":"14 different subspecies. Island life agreed with them. In the absence of significant"},{"x":0.15010660611705437,"t":"predators, they grew to become the largest and longest-living tortoises on the","y":0.38823232238112981,"w":0.73063578287760411,"h":0.019217448464832754,"c":1},{"x":0.15020576441141789,"c":1,"w":0.75720163981119792,"y":0.40694935200540927,"t":"planet, weighing more than 400 kilograms, occasionally exceeding 1.8 metres in","h":0.017469252798666846},{"y":0.42579505306143917,"w":0.39094650268554693,"c":1,"x":0.14814814769319667,"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"length and living for more than a century."},{"c":1,"t":"Before human arrival, the archipelago's tortoises numbered in the hundreds","w":0.71417887369791666,"x":0.15012160984782441,"h":0.019787461513343985,"y":0.45054754615497572},{"y":0.47084805635188987,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"of thousands. From the 17th century onwards, pirates took a few on board for","x":0.15020576812005212,"w":0.73251027425130211,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.71604939778645826,"y":0.48837209286354111,"h":0.017517188693384589,"x":0.1481481405026894,"t":"food, but the arrival of whaling ships in the 1790s saw this exploitation grow"},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.78395060221354174,"c":1,"t":"exponentially. Relatively immobile and capable of surviving for months without food","x":0.15020576881223804,"y":0.50581395334129353},{"x":0.15008628390096732,"y":0.52165723895981642,"c":1,"h":0.020900689249746418,"w":0.73891077677408845,"t":"or water, the tortoises were taken on board these ships to act as food supplies"},{"t":"during long ocean passages. Sometimes, their bodies were processed into high-","y":0.54210836299826515,"w":0.76131688435872391,"h":0.016031172025610885,"c":1,"x":0.15020575530799324},{"x":0.15020575431282954,"y":0.55948174312010868,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"w":0.767489725748698,"t":"grade oil. In total, an estimated 200,000 animals were taken from the archipelago"},{"c":1,"t":"before the 20th century. This historical exploitation was then exacerbated when","x":0.15020575710204848,"y":0.57703488356963994,"w":0.74897120157877595,"h":0.016015764400450716},{"w":0.77589045206705742,"y":0.59366288404506884,"c":1,"x":0.15012682938407076,"t":"settlers came to the islands. They hunted the tortoises and destroyed their habitat","h":0.019374768781718066},{"t":"to clear land for agriculture. They also introduced alien species - ranging from","y":0.6133686690849397,"w":0.73868311564127598,"h":0.015991796172268979,"c":1,"x":0.15020576719279652},{"x":0.15216269918596537,"h":0.021258446296898548,"c":1,"t":"cattle, pigs, goats, rats and dogs to plants and ants - that either prey on the eggs","w":0.76768758138020832,"y":0.62870079804682755},{"w":0.52263371785481771,"x":0.15020577588740594,"t":"and young tortoises or damage or destroy their habitat.","y":0.64811542986088388,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.76131688435872391,"t":"Today, only 11 of the original subspecies survive and of these, several are highly","h":0.01751890058933081,"x":0.15020575531157837,"y":0.67579505305144083},{"w":0.74897120157877595,"x":0.15226337031991571,"y":0.69464075355104016,"c":1,"t":"endangered. In 1989, work began on a tortoise-breeding centre just outside the","h":0.016195524146054185},{"y":0.71051622964985206,"t":"town of Puerto Villamil on Isabela, dedicated to protecting the island's tortoise","x":0.15014760738835367,"w":0.73468994140624999,"h":0.019061923167450034,"c":1},{"t":"populations. The centre's captive-breeding programme proved to be extremely","w":0.74279836018880219,"c":1,"x":0.15226336761650439,"y":0.72819767460548857,"h":0.01744185965530165},{"h":0.017460692757290897,"x":0.15226337062211998,"t":"successtul, and it eventually had to deal with an overpopulation problem.","y":0.74852767948934495,"w":0.69135803222656245,"c":1},{"y":0.77470930217790746,"w":0.78600824991861984,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.15020575157361199,"c":1,"t":"The problem was also a pressing one. Captive-bred tortoises can't be reintroduced"},{"h":0.017484659862181284,"c":1,"y":0.79210836281430674,"w":0.75720163981119792,"t":"into the wild until they're at least five years old and weigh at least 4.5 kilograms,","x":0.15020576968287835},{"x":0.15226337941625787,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"t":"at which point their size and weight - and their hardened shells - are sufficient","y":0.81095406348389132,"w":0.74485595703124996},{"t":"to protect them from predators. But if people wait too long after that point, the","w":0.73045267740885422,"h":0.017506916756062751,"x":0.15226337315079169,"y":0.82848837193311364,"c":1},{"x":0.15226338632137035,"w":0.47736623128255207,"t":"tortoises eventually become too large to transport.","c":1,"y":0.84738372078271229,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"x":0.10699588428937284,"t":"60","w":0.02674897193908693,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.94476744168840554},{"y":0.96768258536995222,"w":0.20824633280436194,"c":1,"x":0.39483721299237268,"h":0.016454192297478354,"t":"leltsresources.org"}]}